  <front>
    <title>Moving the Undeployed TCP Extensions RFC 1072, RFC 1106, RFC 1110, RFC 1145, RFC 1146, RFC 1379, RFC 1644, and RFC 1693 to Historic Status</title>
    <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="6247" stream="IETF"/>
    <author fullname="Lars Eggert" initials="L." surname="Eggert">
      <organization showOnFrontPage="true">Nokia</organization>
      <address/>
    </author>
    <date year="2011" month="May"/>
    <abstract pn="section-abstract">
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">This document reclassifies several TCP extensions that have never
seen widespread use to Historic status.  The affected RFCs are RFC
1072, RFC 1106, RFC 1110, RFC 1145, RFC 1146, RFC 1379, RFC 1644, and
RFC 1693.</t>
    </abstract>
