  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">TCP has a long history, and several proposed TCP extensions have
never seen widespread deployment.  Section 5 of the TCP &quot;roadmap&quot;
document <xref target="RFC4614" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4614"/> already classifies a number of TCP extensions as
Historic and describes the reasons for doing so, but it does not
instruct the RFC Editor and IANA to change the status of these RFCs
in the RFC database and the relevant IANA registries.  The sole
purpose of this document is to do just that.  Please refer to <xref target="RFC4614" section="5" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4614#section-5" derivedContent="RFC4614"/> for justification.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="rfc-editor-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-rfc-editor-considerations">RFC Editor Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">Per this document, the RFC Editor has changed the status of the
following RFCs to Historic <xref target="RFC2026" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2026"/>:</t>
      <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-2-2">
        <li pn="section-2-2.1"><xref target="RFC1072" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1072"/> on &quot;TCP Extensions for Long-Delay Paths&quot;</li>
        <li pn="section-2-2.2"><xref target="RFC1106" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1106"/> and <xref target="RFC1110" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1110"/> related to the &quot;TCP Big Window and Nak
Options&quot;</li>
        <li pn="section-2-2.3"><xref target="RFC1145" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1145"/> and <xref target="RFC1146" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1146"/> related to the &quot;TCP Alternate Checksum
Options&quot;</li>
        <li pn="section-2-2.4"><xref target="RFC1379" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1379"/> and <xref target="RFC1644" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1644"/> on &quot;T/TCP -- Extensions for Transactions
Functional Specification&quot;</li>
        <li pn="section-2-2.5"><xref target="RFC1693" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1693"/> on &quot;An Extension to TCP : Partial Order Service&quot;</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">IANA has marked the TCP options 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, and 15
documented in <xref target="RFC1072" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1072"/>, <xref target="RFC1146" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1146"/>, <xref target="RFC1644" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1644"/>, and <xref target="RFC1693" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1693"/> as
&quot;obsolete&quot; in the &quot;TCP Option Kind Numbers&quot; registry <xref target="TCPOPTREG" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="TCPOPTREG"/>,
with a reference to this RFC.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">As mentioned in <xref target="RFC4614" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4614"/>, the TCP Extensions for Transactions
(T/TCP) <xref target="RFC1379" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1379"/><xref target="RFC1644" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC1644"/> are reported to have security issues
<xref target="DEVIVO" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="DEVIVO"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="acknowledgments" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
